go-deps-group = Dependencies
go-deps-check-updates = Check for newer versions of dependencies
go-deps-check-updates-description = When a go.mod or go.work is opened or changed, asks the module proxy (GOPROXY) for the versions of each required module and the go.mod of its latest version, and go.dev for the latest Go release, at most once an hour: underlines an outdated, retracted or excluded version, strikes out a deprecated module and points out a newer major version and a newer Go. Private and replaced modules (GOPRIVATE, GONOPROXY, GONOSUMDB, replace) are never asked about. Off, the go command's own checks run with GOPROXY=off.
go-deps-check-vulnerabilities = Check dependencies for known vulnerabilities
go-deps-check-vulnerabilities-description = Reads the Go vulnerability database (vuln.go.dev) at most once an hour and the severity of the advisories that apply (api.osv.dev), and underlines a required module with known vulnerabilities.
